 "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le18ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le18ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le18ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le18ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What did you use to do with your families on Christmas when you were young? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: We used to go skating. We would open our presents, then head to the Boston Common skating rink. We would drink hot chocolate and race around for hours!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sounds like fun!"}, {"time": "14000", "image": "engenn6le18ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Have you ever heard of the Freedom Trail? Many families follow the trail on Christmas Day. It's kind of a tradition. Dad, Sis and I always walked the trail. We loved it and it gave Mom a break!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Gilly, Teddy and I wrote and performed plays for Christmas. We put together costumes and wrote out dialogues. We rehearsed for hours. Our various relatives were very good sports."}, {"time": "40000", "image": "engenn6le18ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I haven't had a Christmas like this one for a while. We're a new kind of family don't you think?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, We've had Christmas together for a few years now. We've made our own traditions. I would dread the holidays when I was alone here.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: To many more Christmases together. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Cheers to that!"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Celebrating Christmas"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Remember the Time ... ?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le18ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> are both used to talk about past actions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Gerry</span>: What did you used to do with your families on Christmas when you were young?</br> <span class=\"strong\">Ana</span>: We used to go skating. We would open our presents, then head to the Boston Common skating rink. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> to express something that we often did in the past, but don't do anymore. It is often used to talk about something that was a habit, or a way of life in the past. We we it to contrast past habits with present situations.</br> <span class=\"strong\">Used to</span>  can refer to situations as well as habitual actions.</p> We use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to talk about past actions and habits as well.</br>  Would  only refers to actions, but not situations."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to skate.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't skate anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would skate all day long.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It was my habit to spend all day skating.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense versus The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p>  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I haven't had a Christmas like this one for a while."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you ever heard of the Freedom Trail? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've made our own traditions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Gilly, Teddy and I wrote and performed plays for Christmas."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We put together costumes and wrote out dialogues. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We rehearsed for hours."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Base Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have you ever heard ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"make\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We haven't had ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have had ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The have been ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go skating"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go to an area and skate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We went skating at the local arena. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Christmas."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to race around"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to run all over"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The children race around the house laughing and squealing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to follow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move behind someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We followed the Freedom Trail. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to give someone a break"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to allow someone time to rest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We went out to give Mother a break. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put together"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to construct"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We would put together costumes for our plays. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to rehearse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to practice a play"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We rehearsed the play for hours. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "good sport"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who accepts a bad situation with grace "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our various relatives were always good sports. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dread"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to feel extremely worried or frightened of something."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I dreaded having Christmas alone. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob07aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write about how you or other children felt on Christmas eve."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What you or other children liked doing at Christmas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What activities did you or they do?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Who did you or they see?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "What gifts did you or they do?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I  write about Christmas eve traditions, activities, events and gifts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about activities I or others did on Christmas day."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about who I or others saw."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about gifts I or they received."}]}]}